1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,385
Look.

2
00:00:00,435 --> 00:00:06,644
I just ask: "write the script for a video
about a free logo with AI".

3
00:00:06,694 --> 00:00:09,389
Claude loads my Skill, checks the
buttons on the website,

4
00:00:09,439 --> 00:00:12,712
and gives me a complete script: the
steps, the mistakes, the sources.

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,479
In two minutes, you'll have the same.

6
00:00:14,529 --> 00:00:18,113
No code, and no file.

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:21,557
A Skill is an instruction sheet
that Claude keeps.

8
00:00:21,607 --> 00:00:25,668
When your request matches, it opens it on
its own and follows your rules.

9
00:00:25,718 --> 00:00:28,383
You write it once, and it
works every time.

10
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,607
Step one: check the setting.

11
00:00:30,657 --> 00:00:33,159
Open Settings, then Capabilities.

12
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:36,109
"Create and edit files" must be turned on.

13
00:00:36,159 --> 00:00:37,573
Skills need it.

14
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:41,360
Step two: open Plugins, then
the Skills tab.

15
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:44,650
Click Add, then "Create with Claude".

16
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,794
A conversation opens, with a
sentence already written.

17
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,771
Step three: replace it with your request.

18
00:00:50,821 --> 00:00:53,575
Say what the Skill should do, and how.

19
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:58,504
I want a scriptwriter: a five-second hook,
steps with the exact button,

20
00:00:58,554 --> 00:01:01,835
two common mistakes, then the
time and the cost.

21
00:01:01,885 --> 00:01:05,405
Short sentences, and a source
for every number.

22
00:01:05,455 --> 00:01:06,179
Send it.

23
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:10,433
Step four: Claude writes the Skill
and shows you a card.

24
00:01:10,483 --> 00:01:13,023
Open "Content" to read it.

25
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:15,954
If it looks right, click Save.

26
00:01:16,004 --> 00:01:19,870
The Skill shows up in your
Plugins, with a New label.

27
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,747
Step five: test it.

28
00:01:21,797 --> 00:01:25,029
Open a new conversation and ask normally.

29
00:01:25,079 --> 00:01:26,779
No need to mention the Skill.

30
00:01:26,829 --> 00:01:29,357
Look: "Loading a skill".

31
00:01:29,407 --> 00:01:31,096
Claude found it on its own.

32
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:32,878
Two common mistakes.

33
00:01:32,928 --> 00:01:35,364
One: the Skill never triggers.

34
00:01:35,414 --> 00:01:38,272
It's almost always the
description, too vague.

35
00:01:38,322 --> 00:01:42,652
Ask Claude to rewrite it with the
words you actually type.

36
00:01:42,702 --> 00:01:45,313
Two: you save without reading.

37
00:01:45,363 --> 00:01:49,579
Always open "Content": that's where you see
if it understood your rules.

38
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:55,810
The result: two minutes, zero extra cost, and
an assistant that writes your way,

39
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:56,639
every time.

40
00:01:56,689 --> 00:02:01,646
My exact request and my Skill file are
free in the description.

41
00:02:01,696 --> 00:02:06,882
If you already have a SKILL dot md file, the
Add menu also lets you import it.

42
00:02:06,932 --> 00:02:10,427
Next video: the channel's real
numbers after one week.

43
00:02:10,477 --> 00:02:11,495
Subscribe.

